{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"square-tragic-llama","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe canonical audit run produced 11,480 passes but exposed two reproducible test-environment assumptions. tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py::test_shipped_surfaces_name_no_retired_bridge_command recursively UTF-8-decodes every file under src/rebar, including ignored editor_assets/node_modules binaries such as the Mach-O esbuild executable. tests/unit/test_attestation_signing.py::test_hook_falls_back_to_git_when_env_unset clones the current checkout and fails when it is a shallow promisor clone with unavailable historical objects. These are test-hygiene defects, not runtime failures.\n\n## Plan\n- Make the shipped-surface test enumerate tracked/package-shipped textual inputs rather than arbitrary working-tree artifacts.\n- Make the build-provenance test construct a self-contained minimal Git fixture or explicitly materialize/guard required objects.\n- Add negative controls for an ignored binary under the source tree and for a shallow/partial source checkout.\n- Keep both tests behavioral: stale shipped command tokens and Git-fallback build provenance must still fail when broken.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The shipped-surface contract passes with an ignored non-UTF-8 binary under src/rebar and still fails when the retired token appears in a shipped text file.\n- [ ] The provenance fallback test does not depend on the audit checkout having a complete object database.\n- [ ] The provenance test still proves the wheel embeds git rev-parse --short HEAD when REBAR_BUILD_COMMIT is unset.\n- [ ] Targeted tests pass in full and shallow/promisor checkout fixtures.\n- [ ] No broad decode-error swallowing or unconditional skip weakens either oracle.","id":"def1-9c3c-6802-48bd","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["testing","test-hygiene","git","audit-follow-up"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Harden source-scan and local-clone tests for generated artifacts and partial checkouts"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786212694847436001,"uuid":"32bf10d9-c163-4762-8a31-b44dea0b19c1"}